Package: Loopvelocity
Type: Package
Title: Loop Velocity Estimation from Single-Cell Hi-C
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-08-27
Authors@R: person(given = "Chen", family = "Zhang",
  email = "zhangchen3@u.nus.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates loop velocity, the time derivative of the chromatin
  contact state, from single-cell Hi-C. A loop-extrusion kinetic model
  (one-sided phi(alpha, beta, gamma) and two-sided phi(alpha, theta, gamma)
  parameterizations) is fitted to contacts in ~50kb windows around TAD
  boundaries via a steady-state regression or an EM dynamical model, and
  cell states are extrapolated on embeddings. Provides native readers for
  cool/mcool/scool, 4DN pairs, and sparse contact matrices, plus
  insulation-score TAD boundary calling.
License: GPL-3
Depends: R (>= 4.3), Matrix
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.10), parallel, stats, graphics,
        grDevices, utils, methods
Suggests: hdf5r, strawr, Rtsne, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
